REAL DevOps / SRE Interview Questions 

These are practical scenario-based questions + short answers that are commonly asked in DevOps / Cloud interviews.

------------------------------------------------------------

☁️ Cloud & DevOps Technical Questions:

Q. How do you handle secret management in Kubernetes?
Ans:
- Use Kubernetes Secrets (base64 encoded)
- Integrate with AWS Secrets Manager / HashiCorp Vault
- Enable encryption at rest
- Use IAM Roles (IRSA) instead of hardcoding credentials

------------------------------------------------------------

Q. How does Horizontal Pod Autoscaler (HPA) work?
Ans:
- Scales pods based on CPU/Memory metrics
- Uses Metrics Server
- Formula:
 desired replicas = current replicas × (current metric / target metric)

------------------------------------------------------------

Q. How to debug CrashLoopBackOff?
Ans:
- kubectl logs <pod>
- kubectl describe pod <pod>
- Check env variables, configs, resource limits
- Verify external dependencies (DB/APIs)

------------------------------------------------------------

Q. Cluster Autoscaler vs Karpenter?
Ans:
- Cluster Autoscaler → scales node groups
- Karpenter → dynamic, faster node provisioning
- Karpenter is more cost efficient

------------------------------------------------------------

Q. ALB vs NLB?
Ans:
- ALB → Layer 7 (HTTP/HTTPS, path-based routing)
- NLB → Layer 4 (TCP/UDP, high performance, low latency)

------------------------------------------------------------

🧑‍🔧 Real-Time Scenario Questions:

Q. Pods running but service not accessible?
Ans:
- Check Service type (ClusterIP/NodePort/LoadBalancer)
- Check Ingress / ALB config
- Verify Security Groups & ports
- Check port mismatch

------------------------------------------------------------

Q. Sudden spike in AWS bill?
Ans:
- Check Cost Explorer
- Find unused EC2, EBS, snapshots
- Check auto-scaling issues
- Set budget alerts

------------------------------------------------------------

Q. Deployment failing but old pods working?
Ans:
- New image issue
- ConfigMap/Secret mismatch
- Resource limits issue
- Dependency failures

------------------------------------------------------------

Q. High latency in microservices?
Ans:
- Use tracing tools (X-Ray / Jaeger)
- Identify slow service
- Check DB/API latency
- Analyze CPU/Network usage

------------------------------------------------------------

Q. CI/CD pipeline intermittent failures?
Ans:
- Check network issues
- Runner resource limits
- Dependency version conflicts
- Timeout issues

------------------------------------------------------------

Q. DB CPU high?
Ans:
- Identify slow queries
- Add indexes
- Optimize queries
- Use read replicas / scaling
